{
  "title": "FireAct: Fine-Tuning Language Models for Agents",
  "authors": [
    "Baian Chen",
    "Chang Shu",
    "Ehsan Shareghi",
    "Nigel Collier",
    "Karthik Narasimhan",
    "Shunyu Yao"
  ],
  "year": 2023,
  "arxivId": "2310.05915",
  "abstract": "Recent efforts have augmented language models with external tools or environments, leading to the development of language agents that can reason and act. However, most of these agents rely on few-shot prompting techniques with off-the-shelf language models. This paper investigates and argues for the overlooked direction of fine-tuning language models to obtain language agents, demonstrating significant improvements in performance, efficiency, and robustness.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Language agents use language models to interact with the world. However, existing language models were not developed for agentic use cases, and few-shot prompting has limited learning support. Fine-tuning language models can address these issues, providing more diverse learning support, generalization, and robustness. The proposed FireAct approach fine-tunes language models with agent trajectories generated from multiple tasks and prompting methods.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
