    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "Experiments demonstrate the benefits of fine-tuning language models for agents, including improved performance, efficiency, and robustness. Fine-tuning with FireAct outperforms prompting and other fine-tuning methods, with significant gains in performance and reductions in inference time. The results also show that fine-tuning can improve generalization to new tasks and robustness to noisy or adversarial environments.",
